  "units": [
    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianFlipEnergy.compact_count_gaussian_flip_energy_limit",
      "title": "Actual full Boolean flip-energy Gaussian limit",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6",
          "label": "FIRST S4.E6 GaussianLSI background; SLT GaussianPoincare/Limit.lean L592-L1123 full shift-energy route, especially L1030-L1034 factor4; authored actual Boolean secant alternative",
          "scope": "Authored compact C2 scalar full literal Boolean coordinate-flip energy limit. Same actual count/card/signsum and Gaussian variance1; internally produced derivative-square Gaussian L1, allN full-energy L1 including0, and successor full energy integral limit4. No supplied law/Lip/bound/domain/limit/mass certificate. GaussianLSI, finiteHilbert/noncompact actual SPHMC square-root extension,T2/FIRST4.6/main/work/composition remain OPEN. Focused3163PASS: genuine N0 fullflip domain/zero energy and N1 actual atoms with no half factor; three standard axioms only. Independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit and shared publication remain separate."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d/Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/MeanValue.lean#L152",
          "label": "Pinned actual real mean-value theorem",
          "scope": "Reused compiled primitive; endpoint and domain adapters internally proved."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.GaussianFlipEnergy"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "f:Real->Real, ContDiff Real2 f and HasCompactSupport f are the only analytic premises. Signed f, zero mass and zero f are included.",
        "The actual canonical finite Boolean carrier and literal cardinal-normalized counting law are fixed, not supplied certificates. Function.update flips exactly one coordinate; full energy is the sum over all coordinates with no one-half.",
        "C2compact internally supplies nonnegative bounds B,K for derivative and second derivative, hence global derivative Lipschitz control. Genuine finite-count L1 and Gaussian derivative-square L1 are conclusions.",
        "Only positive successor indices enter the limit. At N0 fullflip energy is an empty sum equal0; the separate derivative observer fprime(0)^2 may be nonzero.",
        "Authored compact scalar GaussianLSI background, not printed FIRST4.6 or a full GaussianLSI proof. Compact GaussianLSI, finite-Hilbert/noncompact extension, T2, main results and expected costs remain open."
      ],
      "statement": "For every real C2 compactly supported f, its derivative squared is integrable for the actual centered variance-one Gaussian. The literal normalized counting measure on all N Boolean coordinates integrates the sum of every squared f-value difference under a single-coordinate Boolean flip, including N=0. Its successor full-energy integral converges to four times the Gaussian derivative-square integral. No law, derivative bound, domain or limit certificate is a caller premise.",
      "formula": "\\mu_N=2^{-N}\\sum_{\\varepsilon\\in\\{0,1\\}^N}\\delta_\\varepsilon,\\quad S_N=N^{-1/2}\\sum_j\\sigma(\\varepsilon_j),\\quad D_N(\\varepsilon)=\\sum_{j=1}^{N}\\left[f(S_N(\\varepsilon^{(j)}))-f(S_N(\\varepsilon))\\right]^2;\\qquad \\int D_{N+1}\\,d\\mu_{N+1}\\longrightarrow4\\int (f\\prime)^2\\,d\\mathcal N(0,1).",
      "boundary": "Authored compact C2 scalar full literal Boolean coordinate-flip energy limit. Same actual count/card/signsum and Gaussian variance1; internally produced derivative-square Gaussian L1, allN full-energy L1 including0, and successor full energy integral limit4. No supplied law/Lip/bound/domain/limit/mass certificate. GaussianLSI, finiteHilbert/noncompact actual SPHMC square-root extension,T2/FIRST4.6/main/work/composition remain OPEN. Focused3163PASS: genuine N0 fullflip domain/zero energy and N1 actual atoms with no half factor; three standard axioms only. Independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit and shared publication remain separate.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Derive compact derivative bounds internally",
          "text": "C2 gives continuous fprime and differentiable fprime. Its derivative is continuous; both derivative supports are contained in the compact support of f. Compact continuous functions have global bounds. Replace these bounds by their maxima with0. The mean-value bound for the second derivative on the real line gives global K-Lipschitz fprime.",
          "formula": "|f\\prime(x)|\\le B,\\quad |f\\prime(y)-f\\prime(x)|\\le K|y-x|,\\qquad B,K\\ge0.",
          "lean": "compact_derivative_bounds; HasCompactSupport.deriv; HasCompactSupport.exists_bound_of_continuous; ContDiff.deriv'; ContDiff.differentiable_deriv_two; Convex.norm_image_sub_le_of_norm_deriv_le"
        },
        {
          "title": "Compute the actual Boolean displacement",
          "text": "Subtract the two literal sign sums. Every unmodified coordinate cancels; the flipped coordinate changes its sign by exactly plus or minus2. Thus for N>0 each displacement has magnitude delta=2/sqrt(N), and N delta squared=4. No artificial energy or supplied displacement certificate is used.",
          "formula": "s_j=S_N(\\varepsilon^{(j)})-S_N(\\varepsilon)=-2\\sigma(\\varepsilon_j)/\\sqrt N,\\quad |s_j|=\\delta_N=2/\\sqrt N,\\quad N\\delta_N^2=4.",
          "lean": "flip_displacement; flip_distance; Function.update_of_ne; Finset.sum_eq_single; Real.sq_sqrt; hr/hdist"
        },
        {
          "title": "Control each true secant and square",
          "text": "Apply the real mean-value theorem with the correctly ordered endpoints. For either sign of the displacement, the secant is fprime at an intermediate point within its length of the original point; the equal-endpoint case is handled directly. Both derivative values have magnitude at mostB. Factor the difference of squares to obtain the cubic displacement error.",
          "formula": "f(y)-f(x)=a(y-x),\\quad |a|\\le B,\\quad |a-f\\prime(x)|\\le K|y-x|;\\quad |[f(y)-f(x)]^2-(f\\prime(x))^2(y-x)^2|\\le2BK|y-x|^3.",
          "lean": "bounded_secant; squared_increment_error; exists_deriv_eq_slope; abs_add_le; abs_mul; mul_le_mul"
        },
        {
          "title": "Sum all coordinates and integrate the uniform error",
          "text": "The triangle inequality for the entire finite sum and N delta squared=4 yield the pointwise full-energy error16BK/sqrt(N). The literal count measure has mass1 by positive finite cardinality. Every energy function is genuinely integrable on this finite probability space, including N0. Derivative-observer L1 comes from actual36. The integrable subtraction identity and probability mass1 transfer the same error to the difference of actual integrals.",
          "formula": "|D_N(\\varepsilon)-4(f\\prime(S_N(\\varepsilon)))^2|\\le16BK/\\sqrt N;\\quad\\left|\\int D_N\\,d\\mu_N-4\\int(f\\prime\\circ S_N)^2\\,d\\mu_N\\right|\\le16BK/\\sqrt N.",
          "lean": "full_flip_pointwise_error; countLaw_probability; Integrable.of_finite; hi/iE/iD; integral_sub; integral_const_mul; norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const"
        },
        {
          "title": "Pass to the actual factor-four Gaussian limit",
          "text": "The scalar inverse square root of the positive successor index tends to0. Squeeze the true integral difference to0. Independently verified36 supplies Gaussian derivative-square L1 and convergence of the same literal count derivative observer. Add four times that limit to the vanishing difference. This proves full-coordinate energy convergence; it supplies no noncompact or cost limit.",
          "formula": "\\int D_{N+1}\\,d\\mu_{N+1}=e_N+4\\int(f\\prime\\circ S_{N+1})^2\\,d\\mu_{N+1},\\quad e_N\\to0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad4\\int(f\\prime)^2\\,d\\gamma.",
          "lean": "GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits; tr/te/tC; Real.tendsto_sqrt_atTop; tendsto_inv_atTop_zero; squeeze_zero_norm; Tendsto.add"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "For every real C2 compactly supported f, its derivative squared is integrable for the actual centered variance-one Gaussian. The literal normalized counting measure on all N Boolean coordinates integrates the sum of every squared f-value difference under a single-coordinate Boolean flip, including N=0. Its successor full-energy integral converges to four times the Gaussian derivative-square integral. No law, derivative bound, domain or limit certificate is a caller premise.",
      "lean_proof": "Derive compact derivative bounds internally; Compute the actual Boolean displacement; Control each true secant and square; Sum all coordinates and integrate the uniform error; Pass to the actual factor-four Gaussian limit",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits"
